  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>Tokenized stocks printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed Value near $2.46B (+0.2% 30D) keeps the lane in a holding pattern\u2014liquidity and platform concentration still dominate. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/regulation/2026-08-20-securitizes-redfearn-sec-innovation-exemption-clarity-act-politics-412298\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Securitize\u2019s Redfearn says SEC held back crypto innovation exemption over Clarity Act politics</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Tokenized stocks remain an early-stage lane:</strong> liquidity and scale are still concentrated in a small set of platforms/networks.</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Securities and broker-rule constraints often set the pace more than listing count, so near-term share stays tied to venues that can actually distribute products. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/regulation/2026-08-19-injective-becomes-sec-registered-transfer-agent-expands-tokenization-push-412225\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Injective becomes SEC-registered transfer agent as it expands tokenization push</a> (The Block).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
